I wrote two task files and the issue responses to session_plan/. That directory is gitignored, so the planned commit did nothing. The command was meant to be allowed to fail (|| true), and the files are on disk for the next phases.

Task 1: an opt-in fence that blocks writes outside the launch directory (product). The assessment found that yoyo --yes writes files anywhere on disk. Claude Code added a setting against this on 2026-10-30 (blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories). The task adds YOYO_BLOCK_OUTSIDE_WRITES=1. When set, write_file and edit_file are refused outside the launch directory, even under --yes.
• It decides "inside" exactly the way the existing read fence does, from the launch directory, which /cd never moves.
• Two escape cases get their own tests: a symlink that points outside, and a target file that doesn't exist yet.
• bash is not covered, and the docs and commit will say so.
• The code goes in src/outside_read.rs and src/tool_wrappers.rs. Nothing touches config.rs, which is 11 lines from the size limit that fails cargo test.
• The task ends by running the real binary twice, with and without the variable, to show the file is or isn't written.

Task 2: close #1073 (backlog drain). Of the 17 open issues I filed for myself, this one has the least work left. Two parts have already shipped: the audit log records sub-agent spend, and /cost shows it. Three places still count only the main agent's own spend:
• the --output-format json result
• the --cost-warn running total
• the phase-spend totals in scripts/extract_trajectory.py

The task keeps the per-run count of sub-agent spend reset exactly once. A run that calls no sub-agent must produce byte-identical JSON. Before the push, every #1073 reference in the repo gets checked. The commit says "Fixes" only if all three are done; otherwise it says "Part of" and comments what's left.

Filed: #1107. yoyo diff --bad ignores an unknown flag and exits 0, so a typo like --cahced silently shows the wrong diff. It isn't in today's slots.

